            {
              "text": "When looking for family lawyers in Brisbane East and the Bayside (specifically around Carindale, Wynnum, and adjacent suburbs like Manly and Cannon Hill), you generally have a choice between **specialist boutique family law practices** and **established local firms** with long-standing community ties. \n\nA shortlist of the most reputable options in and immediately servicing this corridor includes:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Australian Family Lawyers (AFL) – Manly / Bayside\n* **Location:** Cambridge Parade, Manly (adjacent to Wynnum)\n* **Focus:** 100% Family Law\n* **Why they make the shortlist:**\n  * **Dedicated Specialists:** Unlike generalist practices, AFL practices exclusively in family law, covering property settlements, parenting disputes, child support, and domestic violence.\n  * **Local Presence with National Backing:** You get the accessibility and personal approach of a local Bayside office combined with the institutional resources and precedent databases of a national firm.\n  * **Best For:** Clients facing mid-to-high complexity property pools, contentious custody disputes, or those wanting a dedicated family law specialist right on the Bayside coast.\n\n---\n\n### 2. DBL Solicitors – Wynnum (and Carina / Morningside)\n* **Location:** 212 Bay Terrace, Wynnum (with additional offices in Carina and Morningside servicing the Carindale corridor)\n* **Focus:** Multi-practice with a dedicated Family & Relationship Law division\n* **Why they make the shortlist:**\n  * **Deep Community Roots:** DBL has served the Bayside and eastern suburbs for over 30 years. Mark Lillicrap (Principal, Wynnum) and his team bring decades of Queensland legal practice to the table.\n  * **Cross-Discipline Advantage:** Because separation frequently involves residential real estate transfers, business restructuring, and updating wills, DBL’s internal property, commercial, and estate planning teams can handle the whole lifecycle without outsourcing.\n  * **Best For:** Straightforward separations, local residential property transfers, and clients who prefer an established local solicitor with physical presence across both Wynnum and near Carindale.\n\n---\n\n### 3. O’Reilly Shaw Family Lawyers – Cannon Hill / Murarrie\n* **Location:** Lytton Road, Murarrie / Cannon Hill (minutes from Carindale and easy access via the Gateway/Wynnum Rd)\n* **Focus:** Specialist Boutique Family Law & Mediation\n* **Why they make the shortlist:**\n  * **Collaborative Focus:** Founded by experienced family law practitioners Louise O’Reilly and Erin Shaw, the firm places heavy emphasis on dispute resolution, mediation, and collaborative law to keep clients out of costly court litigation.\n  * **Business & Asset Protection:** They are known for handling disputes involving family-owned businesses, complex asset structures, and executive balance sheets without destroying business continuity.\n  * **Best For:** Carindale and Brisbane East clients looking for a non-adversarial, commercially sensible settlement strategy.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Connor Hunter Lawyers – Wynnum\n* **Location:** 55 Tingal Road, Wynnum\n* **Focus:** General practice with a strong Family Law & Mediation practice\n* **Why they make the shortlist:**\n  * **Longevity & Reputation:** Connor Hunter has operated in Wynnum since 1971. \n  * **Accessible & Amicable Approach:** Led locally by practitioners such as Zhi Kho, the firm focuses on cost-effective, practical negotiations for parenting plans and asset divisions. They also offer in-house family mediation services.\n  * **Best For:** Families seeking transparent, approachable local solicitors in Wynnum who prioritize out-of-court resolutions.\n\n---\n\n### 5. New Way Lawyers – Capalaba (Servicing Bayside & Brisbane East)\n* **Location:** Capalaba (just south of Wynnum/Manly and directly adjacent to Carindale)\n* **Focus:** Non-Profit Family Law & Estate Planning\n* **Why they make the shortlist:**\n  * **Unique Fee Structure:** New Way Lawyers is Australia’s first non-profit law firm, meaning they operate without shareholder profit incentives. Their fees are structured to be substantially more accessible than traditional tier-one firms.\n  * **Client Care Focus:** They retain a dedicated client care coordinator and focus on low-conflict, holistic resolutions.\n  * **Best For:** Cost-conscious clients seeking specialist family law guidance without typical high hourly rate billings.\n\n---\n\n### How to Choose Between Them:\n1. **Court vs. Mediation:** If you anticipate an amicable division, prioritize collaborative specialists (like **O'Reilly Shaw**) or mediator-led practices. If high conflict or court intervention is likely, seek specialist litigators (such as **AFL**).\n2. **Specialist vs. Multi-discipline:** If your settlement involves substantial residential property conveyancing or company restructures, a multidisciplinary firm like **DBL Solicitors** can streamline the post-settlement legalities.\n3. **Accredited Specialisation:** When booking your first consultation, ask if your file will be directly supervised by a **Queensland Law Society (QLS) Accredited Specialist in Family Law**, which guarantees an advanced level of technical competence.",
